meta {
  name: Space List Spaces
  type: http
  seq: 144
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.listSpaces?limit=50
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  limit: 50
  ~spaceType: org.example.bucket
  ~spaceDid: did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
  ~cursor:
}

docs {
  The spaces the authenticated account has *written to* or is the authority for:
  { spaces: [{ space, repoRev?, data?, spaceRev? }], cursor? }. "repoRev"/"data" are the
  account's repo head there when it holds one; "spaceRev" appears only for the authority. This
  is deliberately not "spaces I am a member of": a member's PDS only ever learns about a space
  by storing a repo in it.

  Optional "spaceType" and "spaceDid" narrow to a space type / authority DID. With no filters, an
  OAuth caller needs a wildcard "space:" grant; narrowing the query narrows what the grant
  has to cover. The cursor is the last space URI of a full page; a short page ends the walk.
}
